message.content:
This appears to be a CBP ruling on a decorative paperboard house with a light inside, sold around Christmas but with no Christmas motifs. Christmas decorations would fall under 9505.10, but this item has no Christmas motif, so it is likely classified as a festive article under 9505.90 or as an ornamental article of paper under 4823.90. For comparison, lighted ceramic houses have been classed as statuettes and other ornaments under 6913. For paperboard, the candidate is 4823.90.8600 (other articles of paper or paperboard). Alternatively, 9505.90.6000 covers other festive articles. CBP rulings have treated Christmas village houses as Christmas articles when they are used at Christmas, but this item has no Christmas motif and is not specifically Christmas-related, so the festive classification is doubtful. The lighting is also not a lamp, and it is a minor feature. I conclude it is classified as a paper article, 4823.90.86.

Since the house is decorative and not a lamp, and a paperboard article that is not a Christmas article goes to 4823.90, I selected 4823.90.8600, which is the current 10-digit statistical form for "Other: Other" (4823.90.8600 may be 4823.90.8600 as an 8-digit with 2 digits for statistical suffix). I will give 4823.90.8600.

{"hts_code": "4823.90.8600", "reason": "A coated paperboard decorative house with no Christmas motif and only an incidental interior light is not a Christmas festive article or a lamp, so it falls in the residual provision for other articles of paperboard."}
